{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 35, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Hark stranger from distant realms dare to tread where cherry blossoms do dance and rice fields whisper secrets to the wind. Lo I shall weave thee a path most grand through Japan’s fair lands a quill dipped in ink of yore let us commence our noble quest.\n\nUpon the morn of thine arrival in Tokyo the city that ne’er doth sleep let thine eyes feast upon the towers of Shibuya where crowds do swirl like stars in a whirlwind. Thou shalt don thy finest garb and traverse to Shinjuku’s neon lights where restaurants doth glitter like jewels in the night. Let thine tongue savor the delights of ramen so rich it could make a god weep or sushi so fresh it doth taste of the sea’s own breath.\n\nOn the morrow let thy feet carry thee to the Imperial Palace where ancient walls do stand guard over centuries of emperors’ glory. Walk through its gardens where koi do dart beneath thy gaze and let the whispers of history fill thy soul. Then to Asakusa where temples old as time do rise from the earth and the scent of incense and fried dough doth mingle in the air.\n\nBy the third day let thy spirit be lifted to Nikko where forests do stretch to the heavens and shrines carved with dragons’ fury stand sentinel. Marvel at the falls that thunder and the bridges that curve like the backs of gods. Rest thy bones at an onsen where steaming waters doth melt the cares of the world away.\n\nDepart thou eastward to Hakone where Mount Fuji doth loom like a sleeping giant wrapped in mist. Glide across a lake upon a boat so serene thou’lt think thyself in paradise. Gaze upon the mountain’s peak and feel the weight of its sacredness press upon thy heart.\n\nLet thy journey then carry thee to Kyoto the city where dreams are spun from silk and temples are woven into the very soul of the land. Kneel before the golden pavilion and let its glory blind thy eyes. Wander through the bamboo forests of Arashiyama where the wind doth sigh through the stalks like a lover’s secret. Lose thyself in the streets of Gion where geisha do glide like ghosts and lanterns cast their soft glow upon the cobbles.\n\nOnward to Nara where deer with eyes like jewels do prance through ancient temples and emperors of old do watch from their moss-covered tombs. Feed the creatures with sacred crackers and know thou hast touched the divine.\n\nBefore thy return let thy feet tread the streets of Osaka where castles loom over rivers and festivals do burst forth in waves of color and sound. Taste the takoyaki hot from the griddle and let its smoky sweetness ignite thy senses.\n\nAs thy time doth wane let thy heart be filled with the sights and sounds of Japan. Farewell thou noble traveler may thy path ever be blessed with wonder and thy soul forever changed by the magic of this wondrous land.", "logprobs": [{"token": "H", "logprob": -0.1340528428554535}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.004188099876046181}, {"token": " stranger", "logprob": -5.629308700561523}, {"token": " from", "logprob": -1.8856314420700073}, {"token": " distant", "logprob": -2.1861624717712402}, {"token": " realms", "logprob": -2.846384286880493}, {"token": " dare", "logprob": -6.758748531341553}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -2.41780686378479}, {"token": " tread", "logprob": -0.5297935605049133}, {"token": " where", "logprob": -1.5646767616271973}, {"token": " cherry", "logprob": -0.25494062900543213}, {"token": " bloss", "logprob": -0.09692180156707764}, {"token": "oms", "logprob": -0.008748890832066536}, {"token": " do", "logprob": -1.5572035312652588}, {"token": " dance", "logprob": -2.1690521240234375}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.7264869809150696}, {"token": " rice", "logprob": -5.912566184997559}, {"token": " fields", "logprob": -0.10287794470787048}, {"token": " whisper", "logprob": -2.285066604614258}, {"token": " secrets", "logprob": -0.8258320093154907}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -1.459275